{"skill":{"slug":"sag","displayName":"Sag"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545376535,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2093,"sha256":"e9a062586db13baf6088c28779bc21b0ca80f0e96628de8fe91d604a934c12bb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1753,"sha256":"b0aafdef619f3cfc458e705cd62378a3b99eae7ab3e38fdeba7c892e2de55708","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013601736,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"73bd6cdaace830e35b1ce3cc5df68d36c65413c9c417fac9395b335b8b021a1a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/73bd6cdaace830e35b1ce3cc5df68d36c65413c9c417fac9395b335b8b021a1a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: sag\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides an interface for ElevenLabs text-to-speech. The `SKILL.md` instructions are clear, directly related to the tool's stated purpose, and do not contain any prompt injection attempts to mislead the agent into malicious actions. The installation method via `brew` from a custom tap (`steipete/tap/sag`) is a standard practice for distributing CLI tools and does not inherently indicate malicious intent. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159624607},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013601736},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a small, coherent ElevenLabs text-to-speech helper, with the main caution being its unpinned third-party Homebrew CLI install.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Requiring ELEVENLABS_API_KEY is proportionate for an ElevenLabs TTS tool, and the only shown file output is a user-requested audio file under /tmp.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill declares installation of the sag executable from the custom Homebrew tap steipete/tap/sag without a pinned version or digest; this is disclosed and purpose-aligned but carries ordinary supply-chain risk.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are bounded to text-to-speech usage and do not attempt to override agent safety rules, alter unrelated goals, persist memory, hide behavior, or access unrelated data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No artifact-backed persistence, privilege escalation, background service, tool hijacking, destructive action, or broad local indexing behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is to use the sag CLI for ElevenLabs text-to-speech and local playback, and the runtime instructions stay within generating speech, listing voices, and choosing voice/model options.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the sag Homebrew tap and are comfortable giving the resulting CLI access to an ElevenLabs API key. Use a revocable, limited API key where possible, and avoid sending sensitive text for speech generation unless you trust the CLI and ElevenLabs handling of that text.","findings":"[T08] expected: The static scan's Homebrew dependency concern is supported by SKILL.md line 5, but the install is disclosed, directly tied to the skill's TTS purpose, and not evidence that the current package is malicious.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013601736}}}}}